+## D234 An embedding program can require an extension and fix the session model
+
+Summary: An embedding program can fix its interactive session's provider and model and require a compiled extension.
+
+Audience: author
+
+Stock disposition: inert capability. An embedding program's own `main` supplies `cli.MainOptions.HostPolicy`. Both the provider and model ID must be nonempty, and `RequiredFactory` must be present. The host accepts the policy for interactive sessions. Other modes reject it. A nil policy leaves ordinary CLI behavior unchanged.
+
+The host loads the required factory at startup and reloads it with the session. Startup fails if the factory fails. After reload starts, a failed step stops the session while reload still owns terminal input. Other extension factories keep their ordinary error behavior. The factory must be supplied by the binary's own `main` under `docs/specs/extension-factory-trust.md`.
+
+The host copies the fixed identity into the session's model runtime. Model selection and restored state must match it. Chat requests through that runtime check the identity before execution and after request preparation. If a provider payload contains a top-level `model`, its value must equal the fixed model ID. OpenAI-compatible payloads must contain that field. Azure deployment aliases that differ from the fixed model ID are rejected. Provider payload hooks can observe the request, but a change to the serialized payload fails the request. Classifier, image, and deferred provider operations are unavailable on the fixed runtime. Child sessions that use the same runtime inherit its restriction. The extension host rejects load-time model requests and creation of independent host model runtimes.
+
+The host sets `CreateAgentSessionServicesOptions.KeepSession` with `FixedModel`. A Runtime using those Services cancels requests to replace the Session before running its shutdown hooks. This includes new, switch, fork, clone, and import requests from the user or an extension. Tree navigation within the current Session remains available. A caller can create another execution that opens the recorded Session separately.
+
+The policy identifies a provider and model by ID. It does not pin a provider's endpoint or implementation, restrict an extension's own network access, or govern independently created model runtimes. It does not restrict direct calls through provider functions given to trusted in-process Go code. Embedders must select trusted providers and control any separate runtimes they create.
+
+Call-site markers: `coding/services.go`, `coding/session.go`, `coding/runtime_replacement.go`, `coding/fixed_model.go`, `coding/model_runtime_native.go`, `coding/model_runtime_classify.go`, `coding/model_runtime_typed.go`, `coding/cli/cli_runtime_build.go`, `coding/cli/extensions.go`, `coding/cli/policy_graph.go`, and `internal/codingagent/interactive_reload.go`.
+
+Locked by: `TestFixedModelRejectsMutationAndChecksPreparedRequest`, `TestFixedModelRejectsStartupAndBypassedAgentMutation`, `TestFixedModelBlocksPayloadMutationOnRuntimeStream`, `TestFixedModelRejectsWireModelSamplingOverrides`, `TestKeepSessionCancelsReplacementBeforeTeardown`, `TestFixedHostPolicyRejectsIndependentGraphRuntime`, `TestFixedHostPolicyBlocksLoadTimeModelRequests`, `TestRequiredExtensionReloadStopsOnFailure`, `TestRequiredExtensionReloadStopsWhenEarlierStepsFail`, and `TestRequiredExtensionReloadInstallsItsReplacement`.
+
+Remove when: an equivalent host policy exists in upstream Pi or the embedding program no longer needs a required extension and fixed session model.
+
+Approval: the host-policy prerequisite was approved for the P08 member prototype on 2026-11-24.
