+## D235 An extension can read the native host process identity
+
+Summary: An extension can ask its host for the native host process identity.
+
+Audience: author
+
+Stock disposition: inert capability. The host reads process identity only when an extension asks for it.
+
+What: `Context.HostProcessIdentity` in Go, `host_process_identity` in Rust and Python, `ctx-host-process-identity` in Lisp, and `hostProcessIdentity` in TypeScript and JavaScript return the PID, birth, and scope of the host serving the extension connection. Node returns a Promise. The other SDK calls block until the host replies. A retained context uses its original connection and fails if that connection has closed. A fused extension can have the same PID as its host.
+
+On Linux, `birth` is `linux:<start-ticks>`, where the ticks are field 22 of `/proc/self/stat`. `scope` is `linux:<boot-id>:pid:[<inode>]:time:[<inode>]`. On macOS, `birth` is `darwin:<seconds>:<microseconds>` from `kern.proc.pid`, and `scope` is `darwin:<boot-session-uuid>`. The host fails the call if it cannot read or validate the necessary OS evidence. Other platforms return an unsupported error.
+
+The identity contains no credentials. Its fields are meaningful only in the matching OS scope. A caller that watches another process must independently verify that scope and birth, arm its watcher, recheck the identity, and confirm the intended target before treating a later process exit as proof. This call does not establish an exit or close the watcher race by itself.
+
+Call-site markers: `coding/extension/host/subprocess/host.go`, `coding/extension/host/subprocess/host_calls.go`, `coding/extension/host/subprocess/with_session.go`.
+
+Locked by: `TestHostProcessIdentityMatchesLiveLinuxProcess`, `TestLinuxHostIdentityRejectsMissingAndMalformedEvidence`, `TestHostProcessIdentityRejectsArguments`, `TestHostProcessIdentityInFusedExtension`, `TestHostProcessIdentityOnReplacementContext`, `TestHostProcessIdentityBeforeRegistration`, `TestHostProcessIdentityFromFusedFactoryListener`, `TestHostProcessIdentityUsesRetainedConnection`, and the `native-host-identity` SDK scenario.
+
+Remove when: the extension contract no longer needs native host identity.
+
+## D236 An embedding program can bound native interactive input
+
+Summary: An embedding program can select a native interactive input owner through `cli.MainOptions.InputAdmission` independently of model policy.
+
+Audience: author
+
+Stock disposition: inert capability. `coding.NewInputAdmission` requires a pinned Session ID and a positive pending limit. A nil option preserves ordinary input and queue behavior. This capability adds no extension SDK or wire operations.
+
+The native owner publishes an opaque `coding.InputWindow` for one Session incarnation, execution, and settlement phase. `Admit` reserves capacity before posting and returns an opaque ticket. Input handlers see the interactive source. Registered commands are rejected. Handler transformations precede existing skill and prompt-template expansion. Legacy extension sends keep their extension source and skip expansion.
+
+One submission occupies one unit while either its caller reservation or its native posted, preflight, held, or queued work remains live. A canceled active input hook retains that unit until it returns. Queue consumption and every queue removal release native ownership. The host applies the bound to terminal, extension, Session, and Agent user-message producers. A full terminal submission remains editable and displays a refusal. Existing void queue APIs report refusal through a panic in this explicitly selected host. Custom messages retain their separate queue semantics. A custom trigger refused during startup or a closed phase persists its message without opening another execution. Queue restoration keeps image attachments separate from editable caption text and displays their count. Refusal restores the complete terminal draft. Managed cancellation never inserts its content into the terminal editor.
+
+`Await` returns the latched admission result. An interrupted wait leaves the ticket available for reconciliation. `Close` releases its caller reservation and cancels unfinished work. Cancellation before queue commit prevents insertion. Cancellation after commit cannot retract an entry. Admission does not acknowledge persistence or model consumption. A dependent wait from an input callback returns `ErrInputWouldBlock`.
+
+The owner revokes each window before Session settlement preview and handlers, and before final interactive closure. A late hook result cannot enter a newer phase or start an idle turn. Each preflight fixes its execution observation before input handlers run. An idle observation becomes stale if another execution starts during its handlers. A rejected Session borrower cannot revoke the direct Agent or provisional startup window it did not create. A continuation receives new authority. Replacing a Session revokes its prior authority even if the UUID is unchanged.
+
+An explicitly configured initial message receives a provisional startup window. The initial `OnWindow` callback completes off the owner loop before activation and terminal admission. A host can transfer its existing Starting reservations through `Admit` during that callback. Those requests remain in the native preflight FIFO until the configured startup execution promotes that same window once. The initial message is the execution seed and consumes no queued-mailbox reservation. The callback must return before any ticket can commit. Later window publication is asynchronous. Request identity, authentication, replay, and recovery after process death remain the embedding program's responsibility.
+
+Call-site markers: `coding/input_admission.go`, `coding/cli/main.go`, `agent/input_admission.go`, and `internal/codingagent/input_admission.go`.
+
+Locked by: `TestInputAdmissionCapacityIncludesActivePreflight`, `TestInputAdmissionClosureRejectsBlockedPreflight`, `TestInputAdmissionClaimReleaseOrders`, `TestInputAdmissionCancelledHookRemainsChargedUntilUnwind`, `TestInputAdmissionMixedProducersAndVisibleTerminalRefusal`, `TestInputAdmissionTransformHandledAndLegacyExpansion`, `TestInputAdmissionAwaitInterruptionRetainsTicketAndReentrancy`, `TestInputAdmissionReentrantAwaitUsesActualHookContext`, `TestInputAdmissionSessionAndInteractiveClosureFences`, `TestInputAdmissionSameUUIDReplacementRevokesOldAuthority`, `TestInputAdmissionProvisionalStartupRetainsFullMailbox`, `TestInputAdmissionShutdownKeepsOnlyUnwindingHooks`, `TestInputAdmissionShutdownChargesDirectSessionPreflightUntilUnwind`, `TestInputAdmissionCompactionCommandReloadReleasesItsClaim`, and `TestQueueInputClaimsReleaseOnEveryRemoval`.
+
+Remove when: upstream Pi provides equivalent conditional native admission or embedding programs no longer need it.
+
