index af4940d3844072e99fd95d1f0636b8b33aba6305..639b92b566b329973c2e0b7b54ea5a4a71c9154c 100644
--- a/docs/release/0.5.0-release-notes-draft.md
+++ b/docs/release/0.5.0-release-notes-draft.md
@@ -333,5 +333,5 @@
 - `Context.SetEditorComponent` in the Go SDK takes an `EditorFactory` instead of `any`. The old `any` form accepted only nil, so only an extension that passed another value breaks, and `pig extension upgrade` reports it with the fix.
 - The host writes each frame to an extension with one socket write and without allocating, which lowers the cost of every extension call and notification.
-- `pig -p`, `--mode json` and `--mode rpc` runs collect garbage less often when `GOGC` is not set in the environment: the Go GC target is 400 until a collection finds more than 64 MiB live, then the default 100. A short print run then usually finishes without a collection. Measured on Pi-Bolt's headless scenario: about 15% less CPU on a 32-core Linux host and 15% fewer instructions on an Apple M-series Mac, for 2-4 MB more peak memory (up to about 14 MB on a 50-200 KB file write). An RPC session of 200 turns uses about 20% less CPU per turn for about 22 MB more peak memory (Linux arm64, 4 CPUs). Interactive sessions are unchanged, a `GOGC` you set is used as is, and output is unchanged.
+- Plain `pig -p`, `--mode json` and `--mode rpc` runs collect garbage less often when `GOGC` is not set in the environment. The Go GC target is 400 for plain print runs and 150 for JSON or RPC runs until a collection finds more than 64 MiB live, then the default 100. Interactive sessions are unchanged, a `GOGC` you set is used as is, and output is unchanged.
 - Go API: `mcp/oauth` URLs are `oauth.URL` (WHATWG, as Pi's `URL`) instead of `*url.URL`. `StartAuthorization`, `ResourceURLFromServerURL`, `DiscoveryURL.URL`, `OAuthChallenge.ResourceMetadataURL`, `DiscoveryOptions` and `OAuthFlowOptions.AuthorizationServerMetadataURL`, `OAuthClientProvider.RedirectToAuthorization`, `OnRedirect`, and `coding/mcpext`'s `McpOAuthSettings.AuthServerMetadataURL` and `McpSignInPrompt.ShowAuthorizationURL` take or return it. Build one with `oauth.ParseURL`; `Href()` gives the text `url.Parse` accepts.
 - A codemode result or console line holding an unpaired surrogate (`return "\ud800"`, `console.log("\ud800")`) keeps it in the tool result, the json events and the session file as Pi does (the escape `\ud800`), instead of turning it into U+FFFD.
